d row image $\\langle v\\rangle$.\nMoreover $vw^{\\mathsf T}=s$, whence $E^2=E$, and\n$QE^{\\mathsf T}Q^{-1}=E$. The equations $B^*=B$, $N^*=-N$ give\n$BQ=QB^{\\mathsf T}$ and $NQ=-QN^{\\mathsf T}$. Together with the two\nrow equations these imply $BE=EB=E$ and $NE=EN=0$.\nThe implementation also checks these equations directly, together with\ncommutation of $E$ with both saved projections.\n\nA nonzero solution row and a nonsingular six by six minor of the fourteen\nby seven equation matrix certify that this fixed space is exactly one line.\nA nonsingular six by six entry minor of the six proposed algebra matrices\ncertifies their independence. Since the old calculation has already certified\nthe full common commutant dimension as six, and membership of the five old\nmatrices in that commutant, the one new membership check for $E$ completes the\nbasis assertion. No old forty-nine by twenty-five elimination is repeated.\nThe source of the old dimension and all old adjoint relations remains the\nseparately accepted partial certificate, not a new assumption derived from\nits failed six-candidate basis test.\n\nThe line-projector identities, minor criterion and sparse tensor pullback\nare standard linear algebra. Root proposed the present application;\n/root/readback\\_review supplied the conditional algebra proof above;\n/root/ledger\\_preparation supplied this constructive certificate description\nand the new kernel. None is a claim of an Original case before execution.\n\n\\section{The saved coefficient convention and attribution}\nThe accepted projector stores the35 values $\\phi_{abc}$ in increasing\nlexicographic order $0\\le a<b<c<7$. It obtains them by restricting the\nacquired normalized Cayley multiplication and contracting with the acquired\npure symmetric form, and explicitly checks alternation. Existing exact\nmodel joins and normalization acceptance are separate provenance premises.\nFor a row-action matrix $g$, the full pullback coefficient is\n\\[\n (\\Phi^g)_{ijk}\n =\\sum_{0\\le a<b<c<7}\\phi_{abc}\n       \\det g[\\{i,j,k\\},\\{a,b,c\\}],\\qquad i<j<k.\n\\]\nEquivalently it is $\\Phi(\\operatorname{row}_i g,\n\\operatorname{row}_j g,\\operatorname{row}_k g)$ using the full alternating\ntensor. This is the convention already used by the retained direct\ninvariant-form checker, not a new normalization or transpose convention.\n\nThe ring, Cayley and idempotent arguments are standard elementary algebra;\nthe present author supplies this conditional combination and has prior\nauthorship in inherited Source/theory and IO material. The new worker is\nbeing authored by a different agent and requires a distinct Source peer,\nfresh controls, Root ownership and an actual supported application.\nThis note grants no author-time Root flags, execution authority, case\nregistration, whole-manuscript, census, conjecture or Lean credit.\nNo Original numerical array was opened or evaluated to prepare this note.\n\\end{document}\n",
